<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101808" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχεδί-α</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>raft, float</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ σχεδίης πολυδέσμου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.33
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				174
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLille</u>
				25.4
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTeb.</u>
				701.152
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				318
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥσπερ ἐπὶ σχεδίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					85d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ σχεδιῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.2
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. διφθέριναι</span>
			<i>rafts</i> of hides, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				2.4.28
			</span></i>: poet., <i>boat, ship</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				111
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				16.41
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>bridge of boats</i> or <i>pontoons</i>, of the bridge of
			Darius, Epigr. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.88
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				97
			</span></i>, al.; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λινοδέσμῳ ς. πορθμὸν ἀμείψας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					68
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Marm.Par.</u>
				66
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>frame</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ὑπότροχος</span> a
			frame on wheels for moving anything upon, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.Mech.
				10.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>cramp, holdfast</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.Byz.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				4.2
			</span></i>. (In signf. <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i> the word is prob. fem. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχέδιος</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναῦς</span> or
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέφυρα</span>), <i>something knocked
				up off-hand</i>: signf. <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i> must be connected with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχεῖν</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχεδόν</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
